course: dictionary
lesson: 14931
title: Regeneration: growing back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Regeneration means growing back. When a living thing loses a part and then grows a new one, that is regeneration. «After the lizard lost its tail, it slowly grew a new one.» The lizard was not born with a second tail. Through regeneration, it replaced the part it had lost.
explain: Look for clues inside the word. Re- means again, and the rest links to generate, which means to make or produce. So regeneration is making something again. To check, swap in "growing back" or "making again" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word also describes places. «The council planned the regeneration of the old docks, with new homes, shops and parks.» Here regeneration means making an area better and rebuilding it. Science and geography use the same idea: something is made good again.
fact: Regeneration is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say "some regeneration", not "a regeneration".
fact: In science, regeneration is when a living thing grows back a lost part, such as a lizard's tail or a starfish's arm.
fact: «The regeneration of the forest began after the fire, with tiny green shoots.» Regeneration of a forest means it grows back.
fact: Regeneration of a town or area means it is improved and rebuilt, as in urban regeneration.
fact: The swap test works here: "growing back" or "making again" should fit the sentence.
exercise: «The starfish lost one arm, and later a new arm grew in its place.» What is this called? | Erosion | *Regeneration | Camouflage | Migration
exercise: «The council started the regeneration of the old factory area.» What does regeneration mean here? | *Making the area better and rebuilding it | Painting the area a new colour | Knocking the area down and leaving it empty | Moving everyone away from the area
exercise: «The forest was burned, but its regeneration has begun.» What does regeneration of a forest mean? | *A forest growing back | A forest being cut down | A forest turning into a lake | A forest being drawn in a book
test: What does the prefix re- in regeneration mean? | Not | *Again | Under | Very big
test: Which one is an example of regeneration in science? | A river drying up | *A lizard growing back its lost tail | A tree being cut down | A wall falling down
exam: Mia says, «Regeneration is when a town gets a new coat of paint.» Is she right? | No, regeneration means breaking things apart | *No, regeneration means improving and rebuilding an area, not only painting it | Yes, paint is always regeneration | Yes, but only in science lessons
